      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To satisfy audit concerns, maintain detailed records including a purchase receipt, payment proof, and a description of how the chair is specific to your work in a home office. For large expenses, you may want to add tax preparation professional, such as an accountant or tax advisor, to your inner circle to ensure your deductions are well-documented and justified. Making sure the chair's use aligns with IRS guidelines for home office deductions would be important for smooth audit proceedings, to ensure all records demonstrate how this specific purchase strictly benefits business activities.",
